  "mechanisms": [
    "Daylight contains the full color spectrum, with blue light encompassing 50%, making it optimal for positive mental health outcomes.",
    "Daylight eases stress on the eyes, leading to increased information processing and learning ability, and enhanced mental capacity.",
    "Light influences physical health through Vitamin D metabolism, which affects dopamine, noradrenaline, and acetylcholine, neurotransmitters involved in mood disorders, attention deficit disorders, and Alzheimer’s disease.",
    "Natural light entering homes through windows simulates a connection to nature, which can positively affect mental health."
  ],
  "moderators": [
    "Demographic differences (age, marital status, education) between active duty and Veteran populations may influence mental health outcomes and the relationship with built environment factors.",
    "Home characteristics (size, age) may influence mental health scores."
  ],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "Engineers and architects should consider optimizing the built environment to include proper light exposure for positive mental health outcomes.",
    "Changes to the built environment, such as keeping shades open or redesigning facilities for more windows, can be inexpensive if implemented early in the design phase.",
    "Replacing current lightbulbs with full-spectrum fluorescent lighting (FSFL) can be a minor economic impact, as energy consumption is similar to compact fluorescent lamps.",
    "Updating design guidelines for the Department of Defense (DoD) to include full-spectrum fluorescent lighting is a relatively inexpensive change.",
    "Adding more windows is inexpensive at the design phase of construction but would require a large renovation project for existing residences.",
    "A cost-benefit analysis of design changes could help identify the most cost-effective interventions for positive mental health outcomes."
  ],
