  "limitations": [
    "The sample sizes for the Veteran and active duty populations were insufficient to meet the required statistical power (N=783) for validating the HOME survey.",
    "The Housing, Occupancy, Materials and Environment (HOME) survey used in the study was not validated in a previous study.",
    "The populations (active duty and Veterans) were analyzed separately, limiting combined analysis and potentially skewing results due to demographic differences.",
    "There is a stigma in the active duty military that may lead to underreporting of negative mental or physical health issues, potentially affecting survey results.",
    "The natural light rating was self-reported, which may introduce bias, especially given the Veteran population's higher self-reported rating despite living in a sunny location (Denver, CO).",
    "The study lacked a validated, objective measure of natural light in the residences, relying solely on self-reported perceptions.",
    "The required intensity of daylight to positively affect mental health outcomes remains unknown.",
    "Time constraints limited the study, and Veteran data could only be collected from those at the Rocky Mountain VA.",
    "The study is a preliminary analysis, and further research with more participants and validated measures is needed to confirm findings and establish causation."
  ],
